-- title:
--   Orders under the q↦ qᵖ Frobenius on places
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a perfect field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, and let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Write $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC κ Γ` for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\kappa\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\kappa\,p_g$ of $\kappa$-reductions of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma$ (with nonzero denominator). Let $g, r \in F$ satisfy $\mathrm{Frob}(g) = r^p$, where $\mathrm{Frob} =$ `qExpFrobeniusModL κ Γ p` is the $\kappa$-algebra endomorphism of $F$ induced by the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ on Laurent series (the ring homomorphism multiplying all exponents by $p$). Let $u$ be a place of $F$ over $\kappa$, i.e. a valuation subring of $F$ that contains $\kappa$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring. Then the order of $g$ at the place `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL κ Γ p u`, obtained by restricting $u$ along $\mathrm{Frob}$, equals the order of $r$ at $u$; here the order of an element at a place is minus the logarithm of its value under the adic valuation attached to the place.
--
--   This is the place-by-place statement that the $q\mapsto q^p$ Frobenius on the reduction of a modular function field is purely inseparable of degree $p$, so that a $p$-th-power relation transfers orders from a place to its Frobenius pullback. It is used in the analysis of norms of units in the prolongation datum for the model of the modular curve at $p$, where the Frobenius-twisted factor must be read off at each place.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_eq_ord_of_qExpFrobeniusModL_eq_pow.lean

